From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] macro: flush the query cache on the split's back thread

EDEN_NX2_MACRO_QUERY_FLUSH=1 writes held query and semaphore reports out before a native MME DMA
read, or occlusion predicates read stale values. The flush was skipped whenever the GPU split was
active, because the query cache belongs to the split's back and the front must not record into the
Vulkan scheduler (zortos293/Lichii 12db3f599: Kirby Air Riders crashed at its title in
CommandChunk::Record). With EDEN_NX2_SPLIT=2 - the default - that left the fix doing nothing at all,
which is what Eglantine #655's port here says of itself.

Run it through GpuSplit::RunOnBack instead. That is a direct call when it is already on the back,
a defer-and-drain from the front, and an immediate call with no split - the same shape the
neighbouring QueryDma::BeforeRead/AfterBufferFlush calls use behind owns_caches.

What this can break: RunOnBack drains the back and waits, so a flush reached from the front while
the back is busy costs a wait per native MME DMA read. A wrong drain can also expose split
ordering bugs. It stays behind EDEN_NX2_MACRO_QUERY_FLUSH, so nothing changes unless it is set.

Checked: applies to the tree the 0410-0414 stack produces. Not run on a console.

diff --git a/src/video_core/macro.cpp b/src/video_core/macro.cpp
--- a/src/video_core/macro.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/macro.cpp
@@ -1530,6 +1530,12 @@
                             }
                         }
                     }
+                    // EDEN_NX2_MACRO_QUERY_FLUSH=1: write held query reports out before the game
+                    // consumes them, including through the split's back (see below).
+                    static const bool flush_queries = [] {
+                        const char* const flush = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_MACRO_QUERY_FLUSH");
+                        return flush != nullptr && flush[0] != '0';
+                    }();
                     const bool owns_caches = !VideoCommon::GpuSplit::Get().Active() ||
                                              VideoCommon::GpuSplit::OnBackThread();
                     if (owns_caches) {
@@ -1538,6 +1544,15 @@
                         // Flush the report before the game consumes it. A short fence-flush delay
                         // otherwise leaves a stale occlusion value for one frame and flashes white.
                         memory.FlushRegion(source, read_bytes, VideoCommon::CacheType::QueryCache);
+                    } else if (flush_queries) {
+                        // The query cache belongs to the split's back, so the flush above cannot be
+                        // made from the front: recording into the Vulkan scheduler there crashed
+                        // Kirby Air Riders at its title (zortos293/Lichii 12db3f599). Run it on the
+                        // back instead of skipping it, which is what happened under EDEN_NX2_SPLIT=2.
+                        VideoCommon::GpuSplit::Get().RunOnBack([&] {
+                            memory.FlushRegion(source, read_bytes,
+                                               VideoCommon::CacheType::QueryCache);
+                        });
                     }
                     if (memory.IsMemoryDirty(source, read_bytes, VideoCommon::CacheType::BufferCache)) {
                         memory.FlushRegion(source, read_bytes, VideoCommon::CacheType::BufferCache);
